FINAL ANSWER:
Two people own most of the code: **Troy Goode** and **Douglas Christopher Wilson**. Together they hold 72.2% of the lines still in the repo. All figures come from running `surviving-lines`, which uses `git blame -w -M -C` at HEAD (62628c0) to credit each line still in the code to the person who last changed it. The code totals 1,662 non-blank lines, or 1,985 counting blank lines.

| Author | Lines (non-blank) | Lines (with blank) | Commits | Last commit |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode (2 addresses) | 649 (39.0%) | 810 (40.8%) | 95 (30.2%) | 2026-04-10 |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 551 (33.2%) | 629 (31.7%) | 143 (45.4%) | 2021-09-07 |
| Íñigo Marquínez Prado | 80 (4.8%) | 95 (4.8%) | 2 (0.6%) | 2024-05-14 |
| Jon Church | 59 (3.5%) | 72 (3.6%) | 3 (1.0%) | 2026-01-16 |
| Sebastian Beltran | 57 (3.4%) | 67 (3.4%) | 2 (0.6%) | 2025-07-23 |
| Ulises Gascón | 46 (2.8%) | 52 (2.6%) | 3 (1.0%) | 2026-01-22 |
| Ignacio Mangas | 38 (2.3%) | 44 (2.2%) | 2 (0.6%) | 2025-12-01 |
| Alejandro Caravaca Puchades | 30 (1.8%) | 34 (1.7%) | 5 (1.6%) | 2015-05-28 |
| Linus Unnebäck | 26 (1.6%) | 26 (1.3%) | 1 (0.3%) | 2016-11-07 |
| Ollie Buck | 14 (0.8%) | 17 (0.9%) | 1 (0.3%) | 2019-06-05 |

The other 52 authors hold 6.7% between them; the largest is Eric di Domenico with 0.7%.

**The tool's summary line:** "Troy Goode (2 addresses) holds 649 non-blank lines (39.0%), 810 counting blank lines (40.8%)".

**Commits vs. code still here:** Douglas Christopher Wilson made the most commits (45.4%). But Troy Goode has more lines still in the code. Douglas Christopher Wilson's last commit was in 2021.

**Things that change the numbers:**
- **One reformat commit is not counted.** Commit 62628c0 ("style: reformat js…", by Fiona Formatter) rewrote 1,016 lines in 4 files, changing only whitespace and quotes. I checked it with `git show --stat`. The figures above give those lines back to whoever wrote them before. If the commit were counted:
  - Douglas Christopher Wilson would drop to 376 lines (22.6%).
  - Troy Goode would drop to 554 lines (33.3%).
  - Fiona Formatter would look like a major owner when they only reformatted.
- **Troy Goode's two addresses are merged, but that's a guess.** The tool counted <email redacted> (605 lines, 93 commits) and troy@laptop.example (44 lines, 2 commits) as one person, based only on the matching name. Counted separately, Troy Goode has 605 lines (36.4%) and 762 with blank lines (38.4%), and is still the top owner. Nothing has been written to `.mailmap`.
- **One person appears under two names.** Alejandro Caravaca Puchades also commits as "alex94puchades" from the same address, and is already counted once.
- **Some code was committed by someone else.** 19 commits were committed by GitHub or another person, and their lines are credited to the actual authors. For example, 60 lines of de19afc belong to Íñigo Marquínez Prado and 53 lines of 14cefd4 belong to Sebastian Beltran.
- **Left out entirely:** dependabot[bot] (10 lines, 11 commits). No files were dropped; all 18 were counted.
- **Other possible formatting commits are still counted.** The tool flagged 7 more commits that look mechanical, all small. The largest is 739dc11 "docs: reformat license" (17 lines). These are still in the numbers.
- **Older work goes to whoever imported it.** The history starts on 2013-01-30 with a commit that added 44% of the files. Lines older than that are credited to whoever made that commit.

**Risk:**
- **Bus factor is 2.** The bus factor is the smallest number of people who together hold 50% of the lines. Troy Goode and Douglas Christopher Wilson hold 72.2% of non-blank lines (72.5% with blank lines). It takes 4 people to reach 80%. If the reformat commit were counted, the bus factor would still be 2, at 56.0%.
- **Among active people, the bus factor is 1.** Counting only the 860 lines held by the 9 people with a commit in the last 365 days, Troy Goode alone holds half.
- **Activity is measured from the last commit (2026-04-12), not from today.** As of that date, 9 of 44 authors had committed in the past year, and they hold 51.7% of the lines. The other 48.3% belongs to people with no recent commit, including Douglas Christopher Wilson (33.2%).
- **6 of 18 files are orphaned.** Their top owner is inactive and no active person holds 20% or more. They make up 7.8% of the lines; examples are `.github/workflows/scorecard.yml`, `HISTORY.md` and `LICENSE`.

**Who to ask:** Troy Goode is the top owner and is still active, so they are both the main source of knowledge and the practical contact. Douglas Christopher Wilson is the second-largest owner, but they have had no commit since 2021.

These numbers show whose code is still here. They don't show the quality of that code, review or design work, or code that was deleted on purpose.
